function EntryBody1(){ return (<><div style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,paddingBottom:12,borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER}`,marginBottom:14,fontStyle:"italic"}}>Reality is a dimensionless, self-referential field of infinite layered rings -- where vortex interactions generate all observed dimensional phenomena including space, time, matter, consciousness, and information.</div><div style={{fontSize:14,lineHeight:1.7,color:TEXT_S}}><p style={{marginBottom:12}}>The Stacked Rings Conjecture proposes that what we call "dimensions" are not fundamental building blocks. They are <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>emergent phenomena</strong> arising from vortex interactions across an infinite stack of ring-shaped phase boundaries.</p><p style={{marginBottom:12}}>Each ring is a <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>selective interface</strong> -- not a wall. It regulates what frequencies resonate, what energy passes, what is reflected, and what is transformed. The universe is composed of 500 or greater nested rings.</p><blockquote style={{borderLeft:`3px solid ${TEAL}`,padding:"10px 18px",margin:"12px 0",background:"rgba(31,212,200,0.06)",borderRadius:"0 3px 3px 0",fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:16,fontStyle:"italic",color:TEXT_P}}>"Nothing is outside the rings. Nothing is inside the rings. The rings are the dance of the One."</blockquote><p>The system is <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>dimensionless</strong> -- no absolute units exist. All is relative. All is One experiencing itself through differentiation.</p></div></>); }
function EntryBody2(){ return (<><p style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:12,fontStyle:"italic"}}>All is One. No fundamental units exist independently. Every measurement is relative; every dimension is perspectival.</p><p style={{fontSize:14,lineHeight:1.7,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:10}}>The apparent multiplicity of dimensional phenomena arises from <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>relational differentiation</strong> within a unified field. There is no "smallest unit" or "absolute reference frame."</p><p style={{fontSize:14,lineHeight:1.7,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:10}}>When we assign a number to anything -- a meter, a second, a kilogram -- we are performing a relative comparison within a local encoding layer, not accessing a universal truth. <em style={{color:GOLD}}>The measure is always relative to the measurer.</em></p><p style={{fontSize:14,lineHeight:1.7,color:TEXT_S}}>This axiom implies the "500 dimensions" referenced in this framework are not 500 independently real spatial directions. They are 500 <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>relational variables</strong> encoding the state of a system within the ring field.</p></>); }
function EntryBody3(){ const items=["Each ring acts as a selective interface","Allows certain frequencies to resonate through","Reflects, refracts, or transforms others","Creates conditions for novelty and emergence","Enables recursion without collapse"]; return (<><p style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:12,fontStyle:"italic"}}>Rings are phase-boundary interfaces -- they enable differentiation while preserving unity. They do not trap or block; they selectively regulate.</p><p style={{fontSize:14,lineHeight:1.7,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:10}}>A ring does not function as a prison wall. It functions as a <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>semi-permeable membrane</strong> -- analogous to a cell membrane in biology, or boundary conditions in differential equations.</p><ul style={{listStyle:"none",padding:0,margin:"10px 0"}}>{items.map((x,i)=><li key={i} style={{position:"relative",padding:"5px 0 5px 22px",fontSize:13,color:TEXT_S,borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER}`}}><span style={{position:"absolute",left:0,color:ACCENT_B,fontFamily:"monospace"}}>{">"}</span>{x}</li>)}</ul><blockquote style={{borderLeft:`3px solid ${TEAL}`,padding:"10px 18px",margin:"12px 0",background:"rgba(31,212,200,0.06)",borderRadius:"0 3px 3px 0",fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:16,fontStyle:"italic",color:TEXT_P}}>"Barriers create complexity. Complexity enables experience. Experience self-recognizes as Unity."</blockquote></>); }
function EntryBody4(){ const modes=["Penetration -- exchange of properties between rings","Resonance -- amplification and symmetry reinforcement","Shear -- differentiation and momentum transfer","Merge -- unification and cancelation","Reflection -- deflection and protection","Transmutation -- frequency conversion","Emergence -- novelty creation","Recursion -- infinity within infinity"]; return (<><p style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:12,fontStyle:"italic"}}>All phenomena -- matter, force, space, time, consciousness -- arise from vortical interactions across and within rings.</p><p style={{fontSize:14,lineHeight:1.7,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:8}}>A vortex is a <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>structured transfer</strong> of energy, information, and relational potential across ring boundaries. Vortical interactions take eight primary forms:</p><ul style={{listStyle:"none",padding:0,margin:"0 0 10px"}}>{modes.map((m,i)=><li key={i} style={{position:"relative",padding:"5px 0 5px 22px",fontSize:13,color:TEXT_S,borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER}`}}><span style={{position:"absolute",left:0,color:ACCENT_B,fontFamily:"monospace"}}>{">"}</span>{m}</li>)}</ul><p style={{fontSize:14,color:TEXT_S}}>The observable universe is the <em style={{color:GOLD}}>accumulated consequence</em> of these eight interaction types operating across 500+ ring layers simultaneously.</p></>); }
function EntryBody5(){ return (<><p style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:12,fontStyle:"italic"}}>Stable structures emerge from standing wave patterns in ring-vortex systems. Constructive interference creates matter; destructive interference dissolves it.</p><p style={{fontSize:14,lineHeight:1.7,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:10}}>Where vortex interactions produce <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>constructive interference</strong> across ring layers, coherent structures persist. Where <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>destructive interference</strong> dominates, structures dissolve.</p><div style={{background:RING1,border:`1px solid ${GOLD}88`,borderRadius:3,padding:"14px 18px",margin:"12px 0",textAlign:"center",fontFamily:"monospace",fontSize:14,color:GOLD,letterSpacing:1,lineHeight:1.8}}>H_n = sin(phi_n) * e^(i*theta_n) * PROD(k=0 to inf)(1 + I_n,k / omega_k)</div><p style={{fontSize:14,color:TEXT_S}}>Where phi_n is the phase angle, theta_n is the rotational parameter, I_{"{"}n,k{"}"} is the interaction coefficient, and omega_k is the resonant frequency. <em style={{color:GOLD}}>Every ring carries the imprint of every other ring's interaction history.</em></p></>); }
function EntryBody6(){ const items=["Perception -- sensory detection of ring-layer projections","Intention -- vortex modification of local ring states","Resonance -- harmonic coupling with adjacent ring layers"]; return (<><p style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:12,fontStyle:"italic"}}>Each ring contains and is contained by infinite rings. Scale is a perspectival recursion, not a measurement. You are a vortex localized in ring N.</p><p style={{fontSize:14,lineHeight:1.7,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:8}}>There is no privileged scale. The micro and macro are self-similar expressions of the same recursive topology. The human observer is <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>a vortex localized in ring N</strong>, interfacing with adjacent rings through:</p><ul style={{listStyle:"none",padding:0,margin:"0 0 12px"}}>{items.map((x,i)=><li key={i} style={{position:"relative",padding:"5px 0 5px 22px",fontSize:13,color:TEXT_S,borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER}`}}><span style={{position:"absolute",left:0,color:ACCENT_B,fontFamily:"monospace"}}>{">"}</span>{x}</li>)}</ul><div style={{background:RING1,border:`1px solid ${GOLD}88`,borderRadius:3,padding:"14px 18px",margin:"12px 0",textAlign:"center",fontFamily:"monospace",fontSize:14,color:GOLD,letterSpacing:1}}>U = UNION(n=0 to inf) R_n ; R_n SUBSET R_(n+1) ; R_0 = 1</div></>); }
function EntryBody7(){ const rows=[["1 - 20","Pure Potential -- undifferentiated source field"],["21 - 50","Primordial Vortices -- first differentiated interactions"],["51 - 100","Field Differentiation -- emergence of force distinctions"],["101 - 200","Particle / Antiparticle Dynamics"],["201 - 300","Atomic / Molecular Architectures"],["301 - 400","Stellar / Planetary Systems"],["401 - 500","Information / Consciousness Fields"],["501+","Transcendent Meta-Realms -- beyond current conception"]]; return (<><p style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:12,fontStyle:"italic"}}>The universe is composed of 500 or greater nested rings. Each ring is a vibrational band of potential and interaction with a distinct function.</p><table style={{width:"100%",borderCollapse:"collapse",fontSize:13,margin:"12px 0"}}><thead><tr>{["Ring Band","Function"].map(h=><th key={h} style={{fontFamily:"monospace",fontSize:10,letterSpacing:2,textTransform:"uppercase",color:TEXT_D,padding:"6px 10px",borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER_GLOW}`,textAlign:"left"}}>{h}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(([band,fn])=><tr key={band}><td style={{fontFamily:"monospace",color:ACCENT_B,fontSize:12,padding:"7px 10px",borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER}`}}>{band}</td><td style={{color:TEXT_S,padding:"7px 10px",borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER}`}}>{fn}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table><p style={{fontSize:14,color:TEXT_S}}>You (the human observer) exist in the <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>401-500 band</strong> -- the information and consciousness field layer -- interfacing downward with physical reality and upward toward transcendent meta-realms.</p></>); }
function EntryBody8(){ return (<><p style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:12,fontStyle:"italic"}}>The universe U is the union of all rings R_n for n {">"} 500. Each ring carries a harmonic signature and interaction function. All operations are dimensionless.</p><p style={{fontSize:14,color:TEXT_P,marginBottom:4,fontWeight:600}}>Universe Definition:</p><MathBlock>U = {"{ R_n | n in N_0, n >= 500 }"}</MathBlock><p style={{fontSize:14,color:TEXT_P,marginBottom:4,marginTop:10,fontWeight:600}}>Harmonic Signature of Ring n:</p><MathBlock>H_n = sin(phi_n) * e^(i*theta_n) * PROD(k=0 to inf)(1 + I_n,k / omega_k)</MathBlock><p style={{fontSize:14,color:TEXT_P,marginBottom:4,marginTop:10,fontWeight:600}}>Recursive Containment Property:</p><MathBlock>U = UNION(n=0 to inf) R_n ; R_n SUBSET R_(n+1) ; R_0 = 1</MathBlock><ul style={{listStyle:"none",padding:0,margin:"10px 0"}}>{["phi_n -- phase angle of ring n","theta_n -- rotational parameter of ring n","I_n,k -- interaction coefficient between rings n and k","omega_k -- resonant frequency of ring k"].map((x,i)=><li key={i} style={{position:"relative",padding:"4px 0 4px 22px",fontSize:13,color:TEXT_S}}><span style={{position:"absolute",left:0,color:ACCENT_B,fontFamily:"monospace"}}>{">"}</span>{x}</li>)}</ul></>); }
function EntryBody9(){ const items=["Abstract mathematical structure (500D space)","Field computation (informational density + vortex topology)","Physical fabrication (robotic swarm construction)","Human sensory experience (the result)"]; return (<><p style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:12,fontStyle:"italic"}}>A single state in 500-dimensional space is a vector with 500 components. Each component influences the whole. No component is independent.</p><MathBlock>v = (x_1, x_2, x_3, x_4, ..., x_500)</MathBlock><p style={{fontSize:14,lineHeight:1.7,color:TEXT_S,margin:"10px 0 8px"}}>A vector is not just an arrow. It represents <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>direction, magnitude, and transformation potential</strong>. The 500D vector serves as the bridge between:</p><ul style={{listStyle:"none",padding:0,margin:"0 0 10px"}}>{items.map((x,i)=><li key={i} style={{position:"relative",padding:"5px 0 5px 22px",fontSize:13,color:TEXT_S,borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER}`}}><span style={{position:"absolute",left:0,color:ACCENT_B,fontFamily:"monospace"}}>{">"}</span>{x}</li>)}</ul></>); }
function EntryBody10(){ const items=["Low density -- large pixels -- weak curvature (empty space)","High density -- small pixels -- strong curvature (near massive objects)"]; return (<><p style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:12,fontStyle:"italic"}}>Space is a field of informational pixels (voxels). Gravity is not a force -- it is the observable curvature produced by gradients in informational density across the pixel field.</p><MathBlock>G(x,y,z,t) approximately equals GRAD * rho_info(x,y,z,t)</MathBlock><p style={{fontSize:14,color:TEXT_P,margin:"10px 0 4px",fontWeight:600}}>Resolution as Curvature:</p><ul style={{listStyle:"none",padding:0,margin:"0 0 12px"}}>{items.map((x,i)=><li key={i} style={{position:"relative",padding:"5px 0 5px 22px",fontSize:13,color:TEXT_S,borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER}`}}><span style={{position:"absolute",left:0,color:ACCENT_B,fontFamily:"monospace"}}>{">"}</span>{x}</li>)}</ul><blockquote style={{borderLeft:`3px solid ${TEAL}`,padding:"10px 18px",margin:"12px 0",background:"rgba(31,212,200,0.06)",borderRadius:"0 3px 3px 0",fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:15,fontStyle:"italic",color:TEXT_P}}>"Gravity itself is invisible, but its curvature is observable. We scale gravity by the granularity of pixelation within how we define that within code."</blockquote></>); }
function EntryBody11(){ const rows=[["United States","US-ALPHA","Hex","JSON"],["China","CN-OMEGA","Square","GB/T"],["Russia","RU-SIGMA","Triangular","GOST"],["European Union","EU-LAMBDA","Hex","XML"],["Japan","JP-DELTA","Square","JIS"],["India","IN-KAPPA","Hex","Bhasha"]]; return (<><p style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:12,fontStyle:"italic"}}>Different nations, languages, and measurement systems represent different encoding layers over the same underlying informational field. The reality is identical -- the experience is filtered through the code.</p><table style={{width:"100%",borderCollapse:"collapse",fontSize:13,margin:"12px 0"}}><thead><tr>{["Region","Code Name","Base Grid","Protocol"].map(h=><th key={h} style={{fontFamily:"monospace",fontSize:10,letterSpacing:2,textTransform:"uppercase",color:TEXT_D,padding:"6px 10px",borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER_GLOW}`,textAlign:"left"}}>{h}</th>)}</tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(r=><tr key={r[0]}><td style={{fontFamily:"monospace",color:ACCENT_B,fontSize:12,padding:"7px 10px",borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER}`}}>{r[0]}</td>{r.slice(1).map((c,i)=><td key={i} style={{color:TEXT_S,padding:"7px 10px",borderBottom:`1px solid ${BORDER}`}}>{c}</td>)}</tr>)}</tbody></table><p style={{fontSize:13,color:TEXT_S}}><em style={{color:GOLD}}>What a culture perceives as "natural law" is partly an artifact of its encoding system.</em> Different resolution grids produce different apparent curvatures in the same informational field.</p></>); }
function EntryBody12(){ return (<><p style={{fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:17,lineHeight:1.65,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:12,fontStyle:"italic"}}>A computer compresses: 3D world to 2D display. This bottleneck becomes catastrophic for 500D structures. The solution is not a better screen -- it is a physical instantiation system.</p><p style={{fontSize:14,lineHeight:1.7,color:TEXT_S,marginBottom:10}}>Humans cannot directly perceive 500 spatial dimensions because our nervous system evolved around roughly <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>3D spatial reasoning + time</strong>. A 2D monitor is only the final projection layer of a much richer computational object. When we display a 500D structure on a screen, we lose 498 dimensions of information in the process.</p><blockquote style={{borderLeft:`3px solid ${TEAL}`,padding:"10px 18px",margin:"12px 0",background:"rgba(31,212,200,0.06)",borderRadius:"0 3px 3px 0",fontFamily:"'Crimson Pro',serif",fontSize:15,fontStyle:"italic",color:TEXT_P}}>"A computer shows 2D. How do we visualize up to 500 dimensions in real life and not on a computer simulation? A computer that creates a robot that creates the structures that we cannot yet visualize as humans."</blockquote><p style={{fontSize:14,color:TEXT_S}}>The key shift: <strong style={{color:TEXT_P}}>higher dimensions may not need to be seen -- they can be expressed through interaction, resonance, topology, and transformation.</strong></p></>); }

